+Aegis Orchestrator — automation for safety events, policy decisions, and remediation
+
+Overview
+This component receives safety incident events (NATS subject or webhook), asks OPA what to do,
+and triggers remediation or retrain workflows via Argo Workflows. It supports both automatic
+and human-reviewed actions according to policy.
+
+Key pieces
+- Flask webhook endpoint: /webhook (for CI/GitHub -> orchestrator events)
+- NATS subscriber: listens to "safety.incidents" (optional)
+- OPA decision: consults OPA at OPA_URL to get action (auto_remediate | auto_block | require_human)
+- Argo invocation: uses `argo submit --from workflowtemplate/<name>` to launch remediation/retrain
+
+Environment variables (minimum)
+- OPA_URL: http://opa:8181 (OPA REST endpoint)
+- ARGO_NS: aegis-ml
+- ARGO_CLI: path to `argo` binary (default: argo)
+- APPROVER_HUMAN_URL: Optional URL to notify human approvers (Slack webhook or review service)
+- NATS_URL: nats://nats:4222 (optional, if using NATS)
+- ORCHESTRATOR_PORT: port for webhook server (default 8088)
+- ENABLE_NATS: "true" to enable NATS subscriber
+
+How to run (dev)
+1) Install requirements: pip install -r requirements.txt
+2) Run: python3 service.py
+3) Or build/dockerize using Dockerfile and deploy to cluster.
+
+Security note
+- Orchestrator should be deployed in aegis-system namespace and protected by mTLS/ingress rules.
+- OPA & Argo access must be limited to the orchestrator service account.
+
